message: "If you use this result or these tools, please cite them as below."
title: "Moki & Julio: A chaotic invariant set in the loss-modulated class-B laser - a computer-assisted proof"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/laser-chaos"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - class-B laser
  - modulated losses
  - CO2 laser
  - laser rate equations
  - chaos
  - topological entropy
  - covering relations
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
  - CAPD
abstract: >-
  The class-B laser rate equations with modulated losses (Oppo 2025, arXiv:2510.18472, Eq. 27), a two-variable
  description of loss-modulated lasers such as the 1982 Florence CO2 laser, have no rigorous chaos proof that we could
  find; their chaos rests on simulations. At the review's own parameters (mu = 2, eps = 0.04, omega = 1.1, m = 0.0608)
  we prove, with rigorous interval-arithmetic integration (CAPD), 25 covering relations for the once-per-modulation
  map on 24 disjoint sets built along a period-6 saddle orbit and a homoclinic excursion. Hence the map has a compact
  invariant chaotic set: it carries infinitely many periodic orbits and topological entropy at least 0.0537 per
  modulation period, and P^24 has a full two-symbol shift on part of it. Numerically (not proved), the long-run motion
  at these parameters is a stable period-16 cycle in the last steps of the period-doubling cascade, so the proved
  chaos coexists with a periodic attractor. Two independently written checkers, positive and negative controls,
  review-seat cross-checks and a one-command reproduction are included.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23422903"
